ORDINANCE NO.
An ordinance Vacating an Alley Beginning at the southwest cornerof Lot 1, Block 10 of the original iown-of Rector, Arkansas, anddue North along the west boundary line of Lot 1 , 2 and 3, to theNorthwest corner of Lot 3, thence due west 20 feet to theNortheast corner of Lot 10, thence due south along the eastboundary line of Lot 10, 11 and 12, to the southeast corner of Lot12, thence East 20 feet to the southwest corner of Lot 1, the pointof beginning. Authorizing the city Recorder to Record saidOrdinance in the Deed Records of the County.BE IT ORDAINED BY THE CIry COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF RECTOR,ARKANSAS, AS FOLLOWS, TO-WIT:WHEREFORE, a petition was duly filed with the City Council of the City ofRector, Arkansas, on the =day of , .- - \ ,2oos, asking theCity Council to vacate and abandon all that portion of an alley designated analley Beginning at the Southwest Corner of Lot 1, Block 10 of the Original Townof Rector, Arkansas, and due North along the west boundary line of Lot 1, 2 and3, to the Northwest Corner of Lot 3, thence due West 20 feet to the Northeastcorner of Lot 10, thence due south along the east boundary line of Lot 10, 11and 12, to the Southeast Corner of Lot 12, thence East 20 feet to the SouthwestCorner of Lot 1, the point of beginning, now appearing of record in Deed Record
at page in the office of the Circuit Clerk and Ex-Officio Recorder for
the Eastern District of Clay County, Arkansas.WHEREAS, after due notice as required by law, the City Council has, atthe time and place mentioned in the notice, heard all persons desiring to beheard on the question and has ascertained that an alley or the portion thereof,hereinbefore described, has heretofore been dedicated to the public use as analley herein described; that said alley has not been actually used by the publicgenerally for a period of at least five years subsequent to the filing of the plat;that all the owner of the property abutting upon the portion of an alley to bevacated has filed with the Council its written consent to such abandonment; andthe public interest and welfare will not be adversely affected by the abandonmentof such alley.NOW THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED BY THE CITY COUNCIL OF THECIry OF RECTOR, ARKANSAS, AS FOLLOWS, TO-WIT:

endstream
