IN THE MATTER OF THE VACATING OF ANALLEY IN THE CIry OF RECTOR, ARKANSASLOCAI-ED IN THE ORIGINAL TOWN OF RECTORComes now the petitioner, First United Methodist Church, by and throughits attorney, C. Joseph Calvin, and for his relief requests that the City of Rectorvacate a certain alley within the city limits. The petitioner state that it is the soleabutting landowner on each side of the proposed property and that said alley hasnot been used for a period of five years from the date of this petition.Beginning at the southwest corner of Lot 1 , Block 10 of theoriginal rown of Rector, Arkansas, and due North along the westboundary line of Lot 1, 2 and 3, to the Northwest cornei of Lot 3,thence due west 20 feet to the Northeast corner of Lot 10, thencedue South along the east boundary rine of Lot 10, 11 and 12, to the{ioutheast Corner of Lot 12, thence East 20 feet to the SouthwestCorner of Lot 1, the point of beginning.\ryHEREFORE, petitioner prays that it be granted an ordinance vacatingthe above described alley and further that the ordinance be filed with the clerk ofsaid county and that ownership of said alley shall revert to the abutting land
owner trc the center of said alley.
C. JOSEPH CALVINAttorney at LawP O. Box 196201 East Ninth Street
STATE OF ARKANSASCOUNTY OF CLAY
